---
import CodeBlock from '../CodeBlock.astro';
import StepCard from '../StepCard.astro';
---

<div class="sec" id="s6">
  <div class="num">06</div>
  <h2>Optional: review a change in Delta</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Your website already works. Try Delta only if you want conversation and
    changes together for review.
  </p>
  <p>
    Delta's <a href="https://delta.dev/docs/privacy-and-security/agentic-safety"
      >safety docs</a
    > say agents have unrestricted device access, no sandbox and no permission prompts.
    Asking for a plan is not enforced approval. Skip this if you need that protection;
    avoid unfamiliar repositories, whose configuration can run code automatically.
  </p>
  <p>
    Project contents and history <a
      href="https://delta.dev/docs/privacy-and-security/data-storage"
      >sync to Delta's servers</a
    >; agent conversations and relevant code also reach model providers. Use
    only upload-safe practice material. Keep backups outside every agent's
    working project, never open a backup to an agent, and use a separate working
    copy. Backups cannot undo disclosure.
  </p>
  <p>
    Follow Delta's <a href="https://delta.dev/docs/installation"
      >setup instructions</a
    >
    and check <a href="https://delta.dev/docs/agents/models-and-providers"
      >model access</a
    >
    and costs. Paid Zed plans offer metered hosted models; Claude subscription sign-in
    is still marked “coming soon”.
  </p>
  <div class="steps">
    <StepCard number="1" title={'Prepare and open the working copy'}>
      <p>
        Use <code class="i">my-site-delta</code>, the separate working copy from
        the previous section. Delta needs a Git repository: a folder with saved
        history. If needed, use
        <a href="#s3">Claude Code</a> to propose local Git setup and an initial commit.
        Review the plan before proceeding; this is separate from tool permissions.
        Close Claude Code afterward.
      </p>
      <p>
        Add the working copy as a project, then choose Work In → Existing Local
        Checkout. This edits that copy directly; run only one agent at a time.
        An isolated workspace is not a security sandbox either.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="https://delta.dev/docs/concepts/delta-and-git">Git docs</a> allow
        local-only repositories, but the <a
          href="https://delta.dev/docs/concepts/worktrees">worktree docs</a
        > require an origin remote (another Git location). If blocked, stop and ask
        me; do not publish files to continue.
      </p>
    </StepCard>
  </div>
  <CodeBlock
    label={'One small change'}
    code={'Read CLAUDE.md. Add "Maker and photographer" below my name in index.html; use style.css if needed. Change nothing else. No Git commands or publishing; no uploads beyond Delta\'s automatic syncing. Show a short plan and wait for my ok before editing. Then list changed files and checks.'}
    copy
  />
  <div class="steps">
    <StepCard number="2" title={'Review the result'}>
      <p>
        Read the plan before replying. Open Changes with the upper-right diff
        icon to compare additions and removals (a "diff"). Select a line and
        type feedback, or send a normal message. Refresh the working copy's <code
          class="i">index.html</code
        > in your browser; check the words and narrow layout.
      </p>
      <p>
        These edits are already applied, not awaiting acceptance. Close Delta
        before restoring from backup. For help, send redacted error text, not a
        shared thread.
      </p>
    </StepCard>
  </div>
</div>
